# Registers ProductionConfigCheck, which refuses to start the prod profile
# when a required environment variable is missing.
#
# It is here rather than being a @Component or a @Bean because it has to run
# while the Environment is being prepared - before component scanning, before
# any @Configuration class is parsed, and before any @ConditionalOnProperty is
# evaluated. See the class comment for the failure that proved a bean was too
# late even as a BeanFactoryPostProcessor.
org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
  com.example.tracker.config.ProductionConfigCheck
